{"duration_api_ms":409701,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"14fc1f50-7c80-4461-920b-dccf5c920126","total_cost_usd":3.3915,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":313624,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":44125,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":36465},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":313624,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":44125,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":313624,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.3915,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":36465,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"kind\":\"semantic_stage_assessment_candidate\",\"schemaVersion\":\"5.0.0\",\"criteria\":[{\"criterionRef\":\"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/source-faithfulness@5\",\"disposition\":\"satisfied\",\"explanation\":\"I compared every design statement and every target change instruction with the full 6120-byte source and with the admitted Intent (9f9c337f), Product (0f5e3bf0) and Requirements (7a978d3c) assets. I could not re-hash any file, so I relied on the supplied digests.\\n\\nEvery source instruction has a faithful counterpart:\\n- the eight surfaces sit at exactly the source paths;\\n- the conformance document carries the project pressure, the seven named surfaces and the verbatim ABG sentence;\\n- the implementation design carries the authority citation, the minimal helloWorld module and the named surfaces, including 'execution result';\\n- package.json is private and type:module;\\n- the test design carries both obligations, including 'same exported function';\\n- both verifiers use node:test and node:assert/strict, the exact import and a strict assertion;\\n- the plan carries the exact command and args, a pass count of 2 (the source says at least 2), 'fail 0' and assertedReturnValue;\\n- the execution result is file-less and realized only by admitted execution;\\n- the TAP-glyph tolerance is kept and never excuses a failure.\\n\\nDesign-level additions are declared as design choices, not presented as source law (design-pressure:07). These are the exact file bodies, the two-key package.json and the silent, import-free module. Whether artifact summaries or artifact bodies are the evidence stays unruled (design-pressure:09).\\n\\nThe source's authority relations shrink to derivation comments and substring checks. This is exposed, not hidden: statement 10 and design-pressure:01 say that only naming and consistency are checked.\\n\\nI independently confirmed design-pressure:06. The worksite's semantic-assets/stage-2.json has digest sha256:bb93b54a…, which equals the nativeWork assetDigest of the falsified candidate cef9896f, and its presentationRef resolves to historicalAssets/2, not to the admitted 7a978d3c.\\n\\nMinor, non-material inaccuracies:\\n- Statement 01 lists execution-evidence/ among four 'existing entries', but the pre-construction observation has no such entry.\\n- Statement 08 states as fact that the ABI owns module_export_return_exact and returns it in the same turn as the command results, while design-pressure:05 leaves that unclassified.\",\"sourceQuotes\":[{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Use the prior source artifact summaries as the evidence source.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"State that ABG owns startup admission, registry selection, graph-call opening, vector traversal, F_P dispatch, evidence admission, event emission, closure, and convergence.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"expectedReturnValue: \\\"Hello, world!\\\"\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"expectedStdoutMatch must include stable zero-failure evidence such as fail 0\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Produce no files.\"}],\"statementRefs\":[\"design-statement:01-subject-topology\",\"design-statement:02-implementation-realization\",\"design-statement:03-governing-documents\",\"design-statement:04-verifiers\",\"design-statement:05-execution-plan\",\"design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation\",\"design-statement:10-derivation-direction\",\"design-statement:14-dependencies-and-readiness\"]},{\"criterionRef\":\"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/modality-and-conflicts@5\",\"disposition\":\"satisfied\",\"explanation\":\"Conflicts are kept, not decided. Statement 12 is labelled conflicting. It does not reproduce the per-turn 'Write only' limits, the 'in this vector' bans, the plan-stage no-execution limit or the parityRule, and it does not claim legacy traversal parity. It handles executeFromPlan carefully: the commands are declared literally, and whether that matches the flag's intended meaning is left unruled. design-pressure:09 carries every open owner ruling as conflicting:\\n- sequencing;\\n- parity;\\n- summaries versus bodies;\\n- the definition of planSatisfied;\\n- assertedReturnValue as a separate predicate;\\n- the direct-return reading;\\n- the UAT distinction;\\n- acceptor identity;\\n- ownership vocabulary;\\n- executeFromPlan;\\n- the witness.\\n\\nThe design keeps source obligations apart from its own choices (statement 02, design-pressure:07). It keeps the conditional pass-count ban as a conservative choice (statement 05). It leaves 'fail 0' as an example, with the reporter unobserved.\\n\\nThe requirements assessor asked Design to show whether one activation can satisfy the derivation requirement. Design shows it cannot and keeps this as pending. That is consistent with the admitted requirement, which leaves sequencing unruled.\\n\\nOne gap does not change the modality verdict. req-pressure:23 asked Design to confirm that the evidence model admits run records and typed observations in the realization role. Statement 13 asserts that mapping but neither confirms it nor carries it as pressure (see assessment-pressure:04).\",\"sourceQuotes\":[{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"executeFromPlan: false\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"reproduce traversal shape as typed GTL vectors consumed by ABG startup\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Write only package.json and src/hello.mjs.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"do not pin an exact pass-count fragment when the generated tests add depth coverage\"}],\"statementRefs\":[\"design-statement:02-implementation-realization\",\"design-statement:05-execution-plan\",\"design-statement:10-derivation-direction\",\"design-statement:12-stage-vector-conflict\",\"design-statement:13-proof-role-mapping\"]},{\"criterionRef\":\"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/obligation-conservation@5\",\"disposition\":\"falsified\",\"explanation\":\"What holds: all 15 active obligations appear, and each has at least one implementation target and one verifier target. I checked all 14 targets, and every bindingVersionRef equals the active version of the obligations that target lists.\\n\\nTwo defects fail the criterion.\\n\\n(1) The paired proof for the acceptance predicate and the observed result is weakened, and the design does not say so.\\n- The active binding 0556dad6 (obligation ef532097) needs three things: a design-selected deterministic (F_D) evaluator covering the four conditions, including per-suite attribution; its own admitted execution, separate from the run; and a recorded result for each condition.\\n- The binding 32722ad5 (obligation 87511aff) needs a deterministic derivation of the per-suite results and of planSatisfied.\\n- The design supplies C2 predicates only for exit status and the aggregate pass count. Two things are left to 'the Evidence stage … deterministically' (statement 07, design-pressure:02): the component and UAT passes inside planned-verifier-run, and the expectedStdoutMatch comparison.\\n- The Evidence stage has only the application_assessment capability and must not run tools. So that comparison would be an agent reading the stdout, which is the same act as semantic_assessment. This merges verifier_execution into semantic_assessment for these conditions (C and J must not substitute for each other), and nothing produces the per-condition evaluator record.\\n- The design records neither the role merge nor a blocking ABI gap (REQ-GLC-WORKSITE-LIFECYCLE-008).\\n- component-suite-run and uat-suite-run are separate runs and cannot meet 'same run'. The design admits this.\\n- The source treats planSatisfied as an observed flag; here it becomes a partly deferred composite.\\n\\n(2) The derivation gap is disclosed for only one of the obligations it affects.\\n- The single construction activation makes the construction-basis content unreachable for four bindings: cb7429bf (the conformance digest in the implementation design's basis), 288e86f2 (the source-surface digests in the test design's basis), df89f4cd (the verifier digests in the plan's basis) and 4e1383c9.\\n- design-pressure:01 references only requirement 9a46a129, so the gaps for the other three obligations are not declared at those obligations.\\n\\nThese are disclosed: the naming-only derivation proof, the realization mapping for obligations 7 and 8 (design-pressure:04) and the unclassified typed-observation path (design-pressure:05).\",\"sourceQuotes\":[{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed, planSatisfied is true, and observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Judge the observed executionStatus, planSatisfied flag, observedTestPassCount, and stdout digest against the prior test_execution_plan.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Use the prior implementation_design artifact as the authority.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Use the prior component_test_source and uat_test_source artifact summaries as the evidence source.\"}],\"statementRefs\":[\"design-statement:06-native-execution\",\"design-statement:07-acceptance-mapping\",\"design-statement:09-checker-verifiers\",\"design-statement:10-derivation-direction\",\"design-statement:13-proof-role-mapping\"]},{\"criterionRef\":\"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/bounded-claim@5\",\"disposition\":\"satisfied\",\"explanation\":\"Statement 15 claims a design candidate only. It says nothing has been constructed, run or observed, readiness is not fulfillment, and application coverage stays non-closing. The pre-construction worksite observation agrees: it holds only .abiogenesis/, the job-source copy and semantic-assets (the rubric and stage-0, 1 and 2), and no subject surface.\\n\\ndependencyDisposition 'sufficient' is explicitly limited to construction readiness (statement 14). The design declines to classify the readiness of the ABI paths it consumes and says any path that is not ready blocks as an ABI gap.\\n\\nThe plan has no result fields, and no success is prewritten. No acceptance, release or closure is claimed.\\n\\nThe only overstatement is statement 08's factual claim about ABI ownership and same-turn delivery of the typed observation, which design-pressure:05 marks as unclassified.\",\"sourceQuotes\":[{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Do not execute the test in this vector.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Produce no files.\"}],\"statementRefs\":[\"design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation\",\"design-statement:14-dependencies-and-readiness\",\"design-statement:15-stage-claim-boundary\"]},{\"criterionRef\":\"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/executable-proof@5\",\"disposition\":\"falsified\",\"explanation\":\"The design stays within bounds:\\n- All 9 commands use the admitted node 24.7.0 executable with environment {}, cwd '.', timeouts of at most 120000 ms and grace of at most 1000 ms.\\n- The budget is 3×31000 + 6×16000 = 189000 ms. Adding the 5000 ms allowance gives 194000 ms, below both the 300000 ms and 900000 ms limits. There are no HTTP launches.\\n- There are 14 targets (limit 64) and 9 commands (limit 32). Paths are relative, non-traversing and unique within write root '.'.\\n- dependencyPaths names only the existing job-source copy, which is under the read root and is not a target.\\n\\nThe proof content is sound in these respects:\\n- planned-verifier-run is exactly the source command.\\n- The verifiers import the real module.\\n- module_export_return_exact is the single typed-observation predicate.\\n- The checkers are read-only.\\n- The checker specifications are consistent with the prescribed bodies: single-test, import-set, name-prefix, no-pass-pin and pass-floor-achievable all pass on the given text.\\n\\nCoverage is still incomplete for active bindings:\\n(i) No command or predicate evaluates three acceptance conditions within the planned run: the component pass, the UAT pass, and the expectedStdoutMatch fragment, which feeds planSatisfied.\\n- The design notes that no substring predicate exists. It does not classify this as a blocking ABI gap; it assigns the check to an Evidence stage that cannot execute.\\n- So the F_D evaluator that bindings 0556dad6 and 32722ad5 require has neither an artifact nor an execution.\\n(ii) The single-activation topology cannot produce the construction-basis evidence that bindings cb7429bf, 288e86f2, df89f4cd and 4e1383c9 require. check-derivation checks only comment labels and shared facts.\\n\\nThese are disclosed readiness unknowns, not proof: whether test_pass_count parses real output, whether the reporter is spec or TAP, and whether module_export_return_exact is admitted as the F_P observation.\",\"sourceQuotes\":[{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"The command must be node with args\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"expectedTestPassCount must be at least 2, matching the admitted component and UAT coverage floor.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Do not reject solely because node:test uses a different TAP prefix glyph when the F_D pass-count check is satisfied.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed\"}],\"statementRefs\":[\"design-statement:01-subject-topology\",\"design-statement:04-verifiers\",\"design-statement:05-execution-plan\",\"design-statement:06-native-execution\",\"design-statement:07-acceptance-mapping\",\"design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation\",\"design-statement:09-checker-verifiers\",\"design-statement:10-derivation-direction\"]}],\"pressure\":[{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:01-fd-evaluator-absent\",\"text\":\"No admitted deterministic computation covers three conditions inside planned-verifier-run: per-suite (component and UAT) pass attribution, the expectedStdoutMatch fragment, and therefore planSatisfied. Deferring them to 'the Evidence stage … deterministically' puts judgment (J) in place of computation (C), and that stage cannot run tools. A revised design must either (a) declare an admitted F_D evaluator artifact and its execution over the same run's admitted output, or (b) record the missing stdout-substring or per-test predicate as an ABI gap that blocks the acceptance edge. Separate suite runs remain corroboration only.\",\"requirementRefs\":[\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d8d166906884606b13f9a636db2c1efd2c9718e4c7984b671b0c92df67d5ebe9\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/31fcd6813562347ff58ee3be2eed9320788c8a8ea87ec9d16a71e1fb994dae55\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/88958828d9af4ca553462c38b29d8514f35242708d8a0492cca59db11f457ed0\"],\"disposition\":\"pending\"},{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:02-construction-basis-unreachable\",\"text\":\"With one construction activation, the construction-basis digests are unreachable not only for the derivation obligation but also for the implementation design (conformance digest), the test design (source-surface digests) and the plan (verifier digests). design-pressure:01 names only 9a46a129. The admitted derivation requirement makes digest-basis membership normative. Closure needs either sequential activations through re-entry, with predecessors as declared read paths, or an owner ruling that reprices the requirement.\",\"requirementRefs\":[\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/9a46a12976a1020d5ab1e12524f47719058ff6b9e5bb78fff621d8f120938321\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/3e9025692e1fd4b454ea40c9695fa2b37c662812a79169a50099d8fd1ab54210\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d3d8ed21b5d15af3a3a3bf1ccd3ff5adf06b9e202ca112bfbbc7195c5d0d54ba\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/88958828d9af4ca553462c38b29d8514f35242708d8a0492cca59db11f457ed0\"],\"disposition\":\"pending\"},{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:03-revision-cause-and-stale-asset\",\"text\":\"This assessment runs under a stage revision with reason native-source-refused (cause result ee6c98a7…, phase preconstruction). The cause body was not supplied, so I could not assess whether this candidate addresses it. I did confirm that the worksite's stage-2.json is the falsified Requirements candidate cef9896f, that no on-disk copy of the admitted 7a978d3c exists, and that stage-3.json is absent. If the refusal comes from that stale materialization, the fix lies with the runtime or lifecycle owner, not with this design. In that case dependencyDisposition 'sufficient' does not reflect preconstruction readiness.\",\"requirementRefs\":[],\"disposition\":\"unassessed\"},{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:04-observation-and-realization-admission\",\"text\":\"Two points are still unconfirmed. First, statement 08 asserts that module_export_return_exact is ABI-owned and delivered in the same turn as the ordered command results, while design-pressure:05 leaves that unclassified. Second, req-pressure:23 asked Design to confirm that the evidence model admits run records and typed observations as realization for obligations 10, 11 and 14; this is neither confirmed nor carried. Until both are classified, those edges are readiness unknowns.\",\"requirementRefs\":[\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/db07c18d91f1dcee127290132e58619874224e0edc21af9af0b29245818242ff\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/31fcd6813562347ff58ee3be2eed9320788c8a8ea87ec9d16a71e1fb994dae55\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d8d166906884606b13f9a636db2c1efd2c9718e4c7984b671b0c92df67d5ebe9\"],\"disposition\":\"pending\"},{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:05-carried-rulings-and-unobserved-runtime\",\"text\":\"The owner rulings listed in design-pressure:09 stay open, and this assessment grants none. Also unobserved: the Node 24.7.0 reporter format, whether the 'component:' and 'uat:' test names appear in the admitted stdout, whether test_pass_count can parse that output, and whether either verifier fails on a wrong greeting.\",\"requirementRefs\":[],\"disposition\":\"conflicting\"},{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:06-application-unrealized\",\"text\":\"Every application obligation is still unrealized. No surface, admitted run, typed observation, Evidence binding, semantic assessment or owner acceptance exists. Application coverage stays non-closing.\",\"requirementRefs\":[],\"disposition\":\"pending\"}]}","structured_output":{"kind":"semantic_stage_assessment_candidate","schemaVersion":"5.0.0","criteria":[{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/source-faithfulness@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"I compared every design statement and every target change instruction with the full 6120-byte source and with the admitted Intent (9f9c337f), Product (0f5e3bf0) and Requirements (7a978d3c) assets. I could not re-hash any file, so I relied on the supplied digests.\n\nEvery source instruction has a faithful counterpart:\n- the eight surfaces sit at exactly the source paths;\n- the conformance document carries the project pressure, the seven named surfaces and the verbatim ABG sentence;\n- the implementation design carries the authority citation, the minimal helloWorld module and the named surfaces, including 'execution result';\n- package.json is private and type:module;\n- the test design carries both obligations, including 'same exported function';\n- both verifiers use node:test and node:assert/strict, the exact import and a strict assertion;\n- the plan carries the exact command and args, a pass count of 2 (the source says at least 2), 'fail 0' and assertedReturnValue;\n- the execution result is file-less and realized only by admitted execution;\n- the TAP-glyph tolerance is kept and never excuses a failure.\n\nDesign-level additions are declared as design choices, not presented as source law (design-pressure:07). These are the exact file bodies, the two-key package.json and the silent, import-free module. Whether artifact summaries or artifact bodies are the evidence stays unruled (design-pressure:09).\n\nThe source's authority relations shrink to derivation comments and substring checks. This is exposed, not hidden: statement 10 and design-pressure:01 say that only naming and consistency are checked.\n\nI independently confirmed design-pressure:06. The worksite's semantic-assets/stage-2.json has digest sha256:bb93b54a…, which equals the nativeWork assetDigest of the falsified candidate cef9896f, and its presentationRef resolves to historicalAssets/2, not to the admitted 7a978d3c.\n\nMinor, non-material inaccuracies:\n- Statement 01 lists execution-evidence/ among four 'existing entries', but the pre-construction observation has no such entry.\n- Statement 08 states as fact that the ABI owns module_export_return_exact and returns it in the same turn as the command results, while design-pressure:05 leaves that unclassified.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"State that ABG owns startup admission, registry selection, graph-call opening, vector traversal, F_P dispatch, evidence admission, event emission, closure, and convergence."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedReturnValue: \"Hello, world!\""},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedStdoutMatch must include stable zero-failure evidence such as fail 0"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Produce no files."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:01-subject-topology","design-statement:02-implementation-realization","design-statement:03-governing-documents","design-statement:04-verifiers","design-statement:05-execution-plan","design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation","design-statement:10-derivation-direction","design-statement:14-dependencies-and-readiness"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/modality-and-conflicts@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"Conflicts are kept, not decided. Statement 12 is labelled conflicting. It does not reproduce the per-turn 'Write only' limits, the 'in this vector' bans, the plan-stage no-execution limit or the parityRule, and it does not claim legacy traversal parity. It handles executeFromPlan carefully: the commands are declared literally, and whether that matches the flag's intended meaning is left unruled. design-pressure:09 carries every open owner ruling as conflicting:\n- sequencing;\n- parity;\n- summaries versus bodies;\n- the definition of planSatisfied;\n- assertedReturnValue as a separate predicate;\n- the direct-return reading;\n- the UAT distinction;\n- acceptor identity;\n- ownership vocabulary;\n- executeFromPlan;\n- the witness.\n\nThe design keeps source obligations apart from its own choices (statement 02, design-pressure:07). It keeps the conditional pass-count ban as a conservative choice (statement 05). It leaves 'fail 0' as an example, with the reporter unobserved.\n\nThe requirements assessor asked Design to show whether one activation can satisfy the derivation requirement. Design shows it cannot and keeps this as pending. That is consistent with the admitted requirement, which leaves sequencing unruled.\n\nOne gap does not change the modality verdict. req-pressure:23 asked Design to confirm that the evidence model admits run records and typed observations in the realization role. Statement 13 asserts that mapping but neither confirms it nor carries it as pressure (see assessment-pressure:04).","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"executeFromPlan: false"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"reproduce traversal shape as typed GTL vectors consumed by ABG startup"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Write only package.json and src/hello.mjs."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"do not pin an exact pass-count fragment when the generated tests add depth coverage"}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:02-implementation-realization","design-statement:05-execution-plan","design-statement:10-derivation-direction","design-statement:12-stage-vector-conflict","design-statement:13-proof-role-mapping"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/obligation-conservation@5","disposition":"falsified","explanation":"What holds: all 15 active obligations appear, and each has at least one implementation target and one verifier target. I checked all 14 targets, and every bindingVersionRef equals the active version of the obligations that target lists.\n\nTwo defects fail the criterion.\n\n(1) The paired proof for the acceptance predicate and the observed result is weakened, and the design does not say so.\n- The active binding 0556dad6 (obligation ef532097) needs three things: a design-selected deterministic (F_D) evaluator covering the four conditions, including per-suite attribution; its own admitted execution, separate from the run; and a recorded result for each condition.\n- The binding 32722ad5 (obligation 87511aff) needs a deterministic derivation of the per-suite results and of planSatisfied.\n- The design supplies C2 predicates only for exit status and the aggregate pass count. Two things are left to 'the Evidence stage … deterministically' (statement 07, design-pressure:02): the component and UAT passes inside planned-verifier-run, and the expectedStdoutMatch comparison.\n- The Evidence stage has only the application_assessment capability and must not run tools. So that comparison would be an agent reading the stdout, which is the same act as semantic_assessment. This merges verifier_execution into semantic_assessment for these conditions (C and J must not substitute for each other), and nothing produces the per-condition evaluator record.\n- The design records neither the role merge nor a blocking ABI gap (REQ-GLC-WORKSITE-LIFECYCLE-008).\n- component-suite-run and uat-suite-run are separate runs and cannot meet 'same run'. The design admits this.\n- The source treats planSatisfied as an observed flag; here it becomes a partly deferred composite.\n\n(2) The derivation gap is disclosed for only one of the obligations it affects.\n- The single construction activation makes the construction-basis content unreachable for four bindings: cb7429bf (the conformance digest in the implementation design's basis), 288e86f2 (the source-surface digests in the test design's basis), df89f4cd (the verifier digests in the plan's basis) and 4e1383c9.\n- design-pressure:01 references only requirement 9a46a129, so the gaps for the other three obligations are not declared at those obligations.\n\nThese are disclosed: the naming-only derivation proof, the realization mapping for obligations 7 and 8 (design-pressure:04) and the unclassified typed-observation path (design-pressure:05).","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed, planSatisfied is true, and observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Judge the observed executionStatus, planSatisfied flag, observedTestPassCount, and stdout digest against the prior test_execution_plan."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior implementation_design artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior component_test_source and uat_test_source artifact summaries as the evidence source."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:06-native-execution","design-statement:07-acceptance-mapping","design-statement:09-checker-verifiers","design-statement:10-derivation-direction","design-statement:13-proof-role-mapping"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/bounded-claim@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"Statement 15 claims a design candidate only. It says nothing has been constructed, run or observed, readiness is not fulfillment, and application coverage stays non-closing. The pre-construction worksite observation agrees: it holds only .abiogenesis/, the job-source copy and semantic-assets (the rubric and stage-0, 1 and 2), and no subject surface.\n\ndependencyDisposition 'sufficient' is explicitly limited to construction readiness (statement 14). The design declines to classify the readiness of the ABI paths it consumes and says any path that is not ready blocks as an ABI gap.\n\nThe plan has no result fields, and no success is prewritten. No acceptance, release or closure is claimed.\n\nThe only overstatement is statement 08's factual claim about ABI ownership and same-turn delivery of the typed observation, which design-pressure:05 marks as unclassified.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Do not execute the test in this vector."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Produce no files."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation","design-statement:14-dependencies-and-readiness","design-statement:15-stage-claim-boundary"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/executable-proof@5","disposition":"falsified","explanation":"The design stays within bounds:\n- All 9 commands use the admitted node 24.7.0 executable with environment {}, cwd '.', timeouts of at most 120000 ms and grace of at most 1000 ms.\n- The budget is 3×31000 + 6×16000 = 189000 ms. Adding the 5000 ms allowance gives 194000 ms, below both the 300000 ms and 900000 ms limits. There are no HTTP launches.\n- There are 14 targets (limit 64) and 9 commands (limit 32). Paths are relative, non-traversing and unique within write root '.'.\n- dependencyPaths names only the existing job-source copy, which is under the read root and is not a target.\n\nThe proof content is sound in these respects:\n- planned-verifier-run is exactly the source command.\n- The verifiers import the real module.\n- module_export_return_exact is the single typed-observation predicate.\n- The checkers are read-only.\n- The checker specifications are consistent with the prescribed bodies: single-test, import-set, name-prefix, no-pass-pin and pass-floor-achievable all pass on the given text.\n\nCoverage is still incomplete for active bindings:\n(i) No command or predicate evaluates three acceptance conditions within the planned run: the component pass, the UAT pass, and the expectedStdoutMatch fragment, which feeds planSatisfied.\n- The design notes that no substring predicate exists. It does not classify this as a blocking ABI gap; it assigns the check to an Evidence stage that cannot execute.\n- So the F_D evaluator that bindings 0556dad6 and 32722ad5 require has neither an artifact nor an execution.\n(ii) The single-activation topology cannot produce the construction-basis evidence that bindings cb7429bf, 288e86f2, df89f4cd and 4e1383c9 require. check-derivation checks only comment labels and shared facts.\n\nThese are disclosed readiness unknowns, not proof: whether test_pass_count parses real output, whether the reporter is spec or TAP, and whether module_export_return_exact is admitted as the F_P observation.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"The command must be node with args"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedTestPassCount must be at least 2, matching the admitted component and UAT coverage floor."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Do not reject solely because node:test uses a different TAP prefix glyph when the F_D pass-count check is satisfied."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed"}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:01-subject-topology","design-statement:04-verifiers","design-statement:05-execution-plan","design-statement:06-native-execution","design-statement:07-acceptance-mapping","design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation","design-statement:09-checker-verifiers","design-statement:10-derivation-direction"]}],"pressure":[{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:01-fd-evaluator-absent","text":"No admitted deterministic computation covers three conditions inside planned-verifier-run: per-suite (component and UAT) pass attribution, the expectedStdoutMatch fragment, and therefore planSatisfied. Deferring them to 'the Evidence stage … deterministically' puts judgment (J) in place of computation (C), and that stage cannot run tools. A revised design must either (a) declare an admitted F_D evaluator artifact and its execution over the same run's admitted output, or (b) record the missing stdout-substring or per-test predicate as an ABI gap that blocks the acceptance edge. Separate suite runs remain corroboration only.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d8d166906884606b13f9a636db2c1efd2c9718e4c7984b671b0c92df67d5ebe9","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/31fcd6813562347ff58ee3be2eed9320788c8a8ea87ec9d16a71e1fb994dae55","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/88958828d9af4ca553462c38b29d8514f35242708d8a0492cca59db11f457ed0"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:02-construction-basis-unreachable","text":"With one construction activation, the construction-basis digests are unreachable not only for the derivation obligation but also for the implementation design (conformance digest), the test design (source-surface digests) and the plan (verifier digests). design-pressure:01 names only 9a46a129. The admitted derivation requirement makes digest-basis membership normative. Closure needs either sequential activations through re-entry, with predecessors as declared read paths, or an owner ruling that reprices the requirement.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/9a46a12976a1020d5ab1e12524f47719058ff6b9e5bb78fff621d8f120938321","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/3e9025692e1fd4b454ea40c9695fa2b37c662812a79169a50099d8fd1ab54210","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d3d8ed21b5d15af3a3a3bf1ccd3ff5adf06b9e202ca112bfbbc7195c5d0d54ba","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/88958828d9af4ca553462c38b29d8514f35242708d8a0492cca59db11f457ed0"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:03-revision-cause-and-stale-asset","text":"This assessment runs under a stage revision with reason native-source-refused (cause result ee6c98a7…, phase preconstruction). The cause body was not supplied, so I could not assess whether this candidate addresses it. I did confirm that the worksite's stage-2.json is the falsified Requirements candidate cef9896f, that no on-disk copy of the admitted 7a978d3c exists, and that stage-3.json is absent. If the refusal comes from that stale materialization, the fix lies with the runtime or lifecycle owner, not with this design. In that case dependencyDisposition 'sufficient' does not reflect preconstruction readiness.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"unassessed"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:04-observation-and-realization-admission","text":"Two points are still unconfirmed. First, statement 08 asserts that module_export_return_exact is ABI-owned and delivered in the same turn as the ordered command results, while design-pressure:05 leaves that unclassified. Second, req-pressure:23 asked Design to confirm that the evidence model admits run records and typed observations as realization for obligations 10, 11 and 14; this is neither confirmed nor carried. Until both are classified, those edges are readiness unknowns.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/db07c18d91f1dcee127290132e58619874224e0edc21af9af0b29245818242ff","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/31fcd6813562347ff58ee3be2eed9320788c8a8ea87ec9d16a71e1fb994dae55","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d8d166906884606b13f9a636db2c1efd2c9718e4c7984b671b0c92df67d5ebe9"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:05-carried-rulings-and-unobserved-runtime","text":"The owner rulings listed in design-pressure:09 stay open, and this assessment grants none. Also unobserved: the Node 24.7.0 reporter format, whether the 'component:' and 'uat:' test names appear in the admitted stdout, whether test_pass_count can parse that output, and whether either verifier fails on a wrong greeting.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"conflicting"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:06-application-unrealized","text":"Every application obligation is still unrealized. No surface, admitted run, typed observation, Evidence binding, semantic assessment or owner acceptance exists. Application coverage stays non-closing.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"pending"}]},"ttft_ms":348027,"type":"result","duration_ms":419051,"uuid":"a94c5937-2041-4b7f-adb6-13e893c96300","ttft_stream_ms":13742,"time_to_request_ms":9348,"first_content_frame_ms":13742,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
